            <ArticleTitle>A novel SLC34A2 mutation in a patient with pulmonary alveolar microlithiasis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>16047</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1038/hgv.2016.47</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pulmonary alveolar microlithiasis (PAM) is a rare autosomal recessive disease caused by mutations in SLC34A2 and characterized by intra-alveolar accumulation of microliths. We diagnosed a case of PAM in a 27-year-old Japanese female and identified a novel mutation in SLC34A2 (c.1390 G&gt;C [G464R] in exon 12).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
